#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-apps.md
msgid "CAP-APPS Application hosting"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-apps.md
msgid "Product interfaces deployed by CI, behind sign-in, that say which environment they are in."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-apps.md
msgid "Layer L3 · domain: data · depends on: [CAP-NETWORK]{1}, [CAP-DELIVERY]{2}."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-apps.md
msgid "Purpose"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-apps.md
msgid "Host product interfaces that are private by default and say which environment they are in."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-apps.md
msgid "Why"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-apps.md
msgid "A half-switched environment is not partially safe: an application can write to one environment while every label says another. Asking the application which world it believes it is in catches that."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-apps.md
msgid "Interfaces"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-apps.md
msgid "A health endpoint reporting target, catalog and schema, database branch and schema version, build version."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-apps.md
msgid "A versioned interface with a pinned snapshot."
msgstr ""

