#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-apps.md
msgid "CAP-APPS.1"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-apps.md
msgid "MUST"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-apps.md
msgid "Applications sit behind identity-provider sign-in and reach data services privately."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-apps.md
msgid "See CAP-NETWORK.1 and CAP-NETWORK.2 for each application host."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-apps.md
msgid "CAP-APPS.2"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-apps.md
msgid "A health endpoint reports the environment the application believes it is in: target, catalog and schema, database branch and schema version, and build version.{1}*Example:* GET /healthz returns the target, catalog and schema, database branch, schema version and build, so an operator can ask an application which environment it is in."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-apps.md
msgid "Query the endpoint in each environment; every field matches the environment."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-apps.md
msgid "CAP-APPS.3"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-apps.md
msgid "Application interfaces are versioned and change additively; a changed shape is a new route."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-apps.md
msgid "A pinned interface snapshot is compared in CI; removals fail."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-apps.md
msgid "CAP-APPS.4"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-apps.md
msgid "Applications are deployed by CI from a versioned image or artefact."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-apps.md
msgid "Running versions match a tag; no image is pushed from a workstation."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-apps.md
msgid "CAP-APPS.5"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-apps.md
msgid "Interfaces used by staff, learners, guardians or the public meet WCAG 2.2 Level AA (also published as ISO/IEC 40500:2025), checked automatically in CI and by a manual audit for each release."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-apps.md
msgid "An automated accessibility check runs in CI; manual audit findings are tracked."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-apps.md
msgid "CAP-APPS.6"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-apps.md
msgid "SHOULD"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-apps.md
msgid "User-facing text is externalised and translatable, so an interface can be offered in more than one language."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-apps.md
msgid "No user-facing string is hard-coded outside the translation files."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-apps.md
msgid "CAP-APPS.7"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-apps.md
msgid "Data-capture paths work over low bandwidth and tolerate intermittent connectivity."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-apps.md
msgid "Capture flows are tested under throttled and interrupted network conditions."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-apps.md
msgid "CAP-APPS.8"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-apps.md
msgid "Applications that handle T3 or T4 data meet OWASP ASVS 5.0 Level 2."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-apps.md
msgid "The application's verification report cites the requirement identifiers it meets."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-apps.md
msgid "CAP-APPS.9"
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-apps.md
msgid "Applications sign users in with OpenID Connect through the identity provider, and every OAuth deployment follows the OAuth 2.0 Security Best Current Practice (RFC 9700)."
msgstr ""

#: docs/specifications/capabilities/cap-apps.md
msgid "The sign-in configuration is reviewed against RFC 9700; implicit and password grants are disabled."
